<title>TURKEY: Turkey raises sugar beet purchase price 150 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkey raises sugar beet purchase price 150 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's Deputy Prime Minister Tansu Ciller said the government had raised its sugar beet purchase prices 150 percent to 11,000 lira per kg from 4,400 a year earlier, Anatolian news agency reported.</p>
<p>Sugar beet growers had sought a rise in prices to 11,500 per kg.</p>
<p>Farmers had warned that if the price rise for 1997/98 was not adequate Turkey would face a shortfall and imports could follow in calendar year 1998. --Ankara newsroom +90-312-446 2940</p>
</text>
